WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:11.978 --> 00:00:15.215
&gt;&gt; PETE BUTTIGIEG, THANK YOU FOR
JOINING US.

00:00:15.215 --> 00:00:21.054
BUS AND TRAIN SERVICE ALSO
AFFECTED AS THE STORM THREATENS

00:00:21.054 --> 00:00:23.289
TO MAKE TRAVEL IMPOSSIBLE IN
SOME AREAS TODAY.

00:00:23.289 --> 00:00:26.025
YOUR TOP CONCERN RIGHT NOW?
&gt;&gt; WELL, THE TOP CONCERN IS

00:00:26.025 --> 00:00:28.962
ALWAYS SAFETY.
ON THE AVIATION SIDE, OUR

00:00:28.962 --> 00:00:32.398
NATIONAL AVIATION SYSTEM IS
OPERATING BUT IT'S OPERATING

00:00:32.398 --> 00:00:37.503
UNDER ENORMOUS STRAIN.
WHAT YOU HAVE IS MULTIPLE ISSUES

00:00:37.503 --> 00:00:41.341
ACROSS DIFFERENT AREAS OF THE
AIRSPACE.

00:00:41.341 --> 00:00:44.477
IN THE NORTHWEST, SNOW IS
AFFECTING SEATTLE, PORTLAND AND

00:00:44.477 --> 00:00:48.481
THAT AREA.
ON THE EAST COAST DOWN TOWARD

00:00:48.481 --> 00:00:52.985
ATLANTA, WIND IS THE MAIN ISSUE.
AND AS YOUR CORRESPONDENT

00:00:52.985 --> 00:00:57.857
REPORTED IN THE MIDDLE OF THE
COUNTRY, IT'S REALLY ABOUT THAT

00:00:57.857 --> 00:00:59.392
FRIGID TEMPERATURE YOU'RE
SEEING.

00:00:59.392 --> 00:01:01.794
THAT LIMITS THE GROUND CREW FROM
YOU OPERATING.

00:01:01.794 --> 00:01:09.035
THEY HAVE A LOT OF WINTER
WEATHER GEAR BUT THERE'S ONLY SO

00:01:09.035 --> 00:01:18.545
LONG THOSE WORKERS CAN BE ON THE
GROUND SERVICING BEFORE IT'S A

00:01:18.545 --> 00:01:22.916
SAFE ISSUE.
I CONSIDER ANYTHING ABOVE ABOUT

00:01:22.916 --> 00:01:26.953
2% TO BE A HIGH RATE OF
CANCELLATION AND AS IT WAS

00:01:26.953 --> 00:01:30.356
REPORTED TODAY, WE'RE ALREADY
ABOVE THE NUMBER OF

00:01:30.356 --> 00:01:33.560
CANCELLATIONS WE SAW YESTERDAY.
SO THE AVIATION PICTURE, YOU'LL

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:38.264
SEE A LOT OF DISRUPTIONS.
ENCOURAGE PEOPLE TO STAY IN

00:01:38.264 --> 00:01:41.767
CLOSE TOUCH WITH THEIR AIRLINE
BUT FROM A SAFETY PERSPECTIVE,

00:01:41.767 --> 00:01:43.937
THE THING YOU'LL MOST WORRIED
ABOUT IS THE ROADWAYS.

00:01:43.937 --> 00:01:49.008
YOU HAVE A LOT OF DRIVERS MAYBE
NOT USED TO DRIVING IN WINTER

00:01:49.008 --> 00:01:52.212
CONDITIONS, TRAVELING TO A PLACE
YOU'RE NOT USED TO DRIVING TO

00:01:52.212 --> 00:01:55.014
VISIT RELATIVES.
I KNOW WE ALL WANT TO GET TO OUR

00:01:55.014 --> 00:01:58.651
LOVED ONES FOR THE HOLIDAYS BUT
PLEASE, PLEASE PAY CLOSE

00:01:58.651 --> 00:02:01.054
ATTENTION TO WHAT LOCAL
AUTHORITIES ARE SAYING.

00:02:01.054 --> 00:02:04.624
IF THAT YOUR SAYING IT'S NOT
SAFE TO DRIVE, IT'S NOT SAFE TO

00:02:04.624 --> 00:02:05.758
DRIVE.
NO MATTER HOW MUCH YOU WANT TO

00:02:05.758 --> 00:02:10.563
BE QUICKLY TO YOUR LOVED ONES,
MAKE SURE YOU GET THERE SAFE.

00:02:10.563 --> 00:02:13.966
&gt;&gt; I'M GLAD YOU'RE STRESSING THE
ROAD BECAUSE THAT'S HOW MOST

00:02:13.966 --> 00:02:18.337
PEOPLE TRAVEL IS ON THE ROADS.
IT'S NOT NECESSARILY AIR TRAVEL,

00:02:18.337 --> 00:02:22.208
THOUGH THAT IS VERY IMPORTANT.
&gt;&gt; PRESIDENT BIDEN IS URGING

00:02:22.208 --> 00:02:26.012
AMERICANS TO STAY OFF THE ROADS
IN PLACES WHERE THE WEATHER IS

00:02:26.012 --> 00:02:29.415
BAD, AS YOU JUST HAVE AS WELL.
THE CANCELLATIONS LIKELY TO PUSH

00:02:29.415 --> 00:02:33.653
SOME FAMILIES TO DRIVE EVEN MORE
AND TO DRIVE HOME FOR THE

00:02:33.653 --> 00:02:37.690
HOLIDAYS INSTEAD.
HOW IMPORTANT IS IT TO HEED THE

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:40.793
WARNINGS THAT THE PRESIDENT IS
GIVING AND THAT YOU JUST GAVE

00:02:40.793 --> 00:02:46.266
HERE ON OUR AIR AS WELL?
&gt;&gt; WELL, LOTS OF THINGS ARE SO

00:02:46.266 --> 00:02:48.468
IMPORTANT TO US AROUND THE
HOLIDAYS.

00:02:48.468 --> 00:02:51.638
OUR TRADITIONS, OUR LOVED ONES.
BUT OF COURSE THE MOST IMPORTANT

00:02:51.638 --> 00:02:56.409
THING IS TO BE SAFE, TO BE ALIVE
AND WELL FOR YOUR LOVED ONES AND

00:02:56.409 --> 00:03:01.214
THAT MEANS MAKING SMART CHOICES
WHEN IT COMES TO DRIVING

00:03:01.214 --> 00:03:05.184
CONDITIONS AND ROAD CONDITIONS.
IF THE INDICATION FROM THE

00:03:05.184 --> 00:03:08.388
FORECASTS AND LOCAL AUTHORITIES
IS THAT YOU CAN DRIVE BUT YOU

00:03:08.388 --> 00:03:10.857
NEED TO DO IT WITH CAUTION, TAKE
THOSE STEPS.

00:03:10.857 --> 00:03:13.259
WE'VE GOT RECOMMENDATIONS ON OUR
WEB SITE.

00:03:13.259 --> 00:03:16.362
YOU CAN SEE THAT WITH LOCAL
AUTHORITIES, TOO, ABOUT HOW TO

00:03:16.362 --> 00:03:19.599
MAKE SURE YOUR CAR IS EQUIPPED
FOR WINTER WEATHER, THAT YOU ARE

00:03:19.599 --> 00:03:23.769
USING A CAR SEAT IN A WAY THAT'S
SAFE WITH THE BLANKET AND

00:03:23.769 --> 00:03:28.341
JACKETS ON THE OUTSIDE OF THE
STRAPS, NOT THE INSIDE, THOSE

00:03:28.341 --> 00:03:30.376
KIND OF STEPS THAT WILL MAKE IT
SAFE.

00:03:30.376 --> 00:03:32.478
BUT IF THEY'RE SAYING DON'T
DRIVE, DON'T DRIVE.

00:03:32.478 --> 00:03:34.780
THE PRESIDENT INDICATED HOW
SERIOUS THIS IS.

00:03:34.780 --> 00:03:38.785
WE'RE SEEING THINGS LIKE I-90
ACTUALLY CLOSED OUTRIGHT IN

00:03:38.785 --> 00:03:42.055
PARTS OF SOUTH DAKOTA AND
MINNESOTA LAST I SAW.

00:03:42.055 --> 00:03:45.558
THAT IS NOT A STEP THAT
AUTHORITIES TAKE LIGHTLY,

00:03:45.558 --> 00:03:47.927
CLOSING AN INTERSTATE.
YOU REALLY WANT TO PAY ATTENTION

00:03:47.927 --> 00:03:50.396
TO LOCAL WARNINGS BECAUSE THESE
TEMPERATURES THAT WE'RE SEEING,

00:03:50.396 --> 00:03:53.933
ESPECIALLY IN THE MIDDLE PART OF
THE COUNTRY, THAT CAN TURN AN

00:03:53.933 --> 00:03:57.203
ORDINARY FENDER BENDER INTO
SOMETHING MUCH MORE DANGEROUS.

00:03:57.203 --> 00:04:01.341
&gt;&gt; I KNOW YOU'RE THE
TRANSPORTATION SECRETARY BUT I

00:04:01.341 --> 00:04:03.776
ALSO WANT TO TALK ABOUT
INFRASTRUCTURE BECAUSE THE TWO

00:04:03.776 --> 00:04:07.113
DO CONNECT.
CRAIG MILLER, PROFESSOR OF

00:04:07.113 --> 00:04:13.019
ELECTRICAL AND COMPUTER
ENGINEERING AT CARNEGIE MELLON

00:04:13.019 --> 00:04:16.756
UNIVERSITY, HE TALKED ABOUT THE
STRESS ON OUR ELECTRICAL GRIDS

00:04:16.756 --> 00:04:19.025
AND THE STRESS THAT WORKERS
CAN'T GET OUT THERE IN THE

00:04:19.025 --> 00:04:24.897
MIDDLE OF IT, IT'S GOING TO TAKE
SOME TIME, IT HAS TO WARM UP A

00:04:24.897 --> 00:04:29.802
LITTLE FOR THEM TO GET OUT THERE
AND THE STRESS IT PUTS ON THE

00:04:29.802 --> 00:04:33.439
SYSTEM WHEN THE POWER COMES BACK
ON BECAUSE EVERYONE HAS THEIR

00:04:33.439 --> 00:04:35.708
POWER ON AND WHAT HAVE YOU, CAN
YOU SPEAK TO THAT?

00:04:35.708 --> 00:04:40.546
&gt;&gt; I DON'T WANT TO GET TOO FAR
OUTSIDE OF MY EXPERTISE BUT THIS

00:04:40.546 --> 00:04:45.585
IS ANOTHER AREA YOU WANT TO PAY
ATTENTION TO WHAT LOCAL

00:04:45.585 --> 00:04:47.353
AUTHORITIES AND LOCAL UTILITIES
ARE SAYING.

00:04:47.353 --> 00:04:52.592
JUST AS WE HAVE EXTRAORDINARY
TRANSPORTATION WORKERS, WHO ARE

00:04:52.592 --> 00:04:56.229
EVEN IN THESE EXTREME CONDITIONS
HELPING YOU GET TO WHERE YOU

00:04:56.229 --> 00:05:00.666
NEED TO BE AND GETTING PACKAGES
TO WHERE THEY NEED TO BE.

00:05:00.666 --> 00:05:04.370
WHEN YOU DO HAVE THESE OUTAGES,
IT EXTRAORDINARY WHAT THE LINE

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:08.508
WORKERS AND OTHERS GO THROUGH IN
ORDER TO QUICKLY RESTORE POWER.

00:05:08.508 --> 00:05:12.445
IMPORTANT TO LISTEN TO ANY LOCAL
ANNOUNCEMENTS ABOUT HOW TO MAKE

00:05:12.445 --> 00:05:18.050
THINGS A LITTLE BIT EASIER FOR
THEM.

00:05:18.050 --> 00:05:21.387
EVERYONE'S PRIORITY IS TO KEEP
EVERYBODY UP AND RUNNING AND

00:05:21.387 --> 00:05:26.959
KEEP PEOPLE SAFE.
&gt;&gt; AS A FORMER MAYOR, I KNOW UP

00:05:26.959 --> 00:05:28.428
WOULD KNOW HOW TO ANSWER THAT
QUESTION.

00:05:28.428 --> 00:05:34.434
UP HAD TO DEAL WITH THAT IN THAT
ROLE AS WELL.

00:05:34.434 --> 00:05:36.502
THANK YOU AND MERRY CHRISTMAS TO
YOU AND YOURS.

00:05:36.502 --> 00:05:38.704
&gt;&gt; THANK YOU.
TAKE CARE.

00:05:38.704 --> 00:05:45.244
&gt;&gt; LET'S GO TO REPORTER JEREMY
PIERRE, WHO IS LIVE FOR US IN

00:05:45.244 --> 00:05:48.681
MEMPHIS, TENNESSEE.
WIND CHILLS CLOCKED AT NEGATIVE

00:05:48.681 --> 00:05:51.818
18.
THAT'S NOT NORMAL FOR MEMPHIS.

00:05:51.818 --> 00:05:55.555
HOW ARE THINGS GOING THERE?
&gt;&gt; Reporter: DEFINITELY NOT A

00:05:55.555 --> 00:05:59.091
TYPICAL DAY HERE IN THE CITY OF
MEMPHIS AND IT'S SHOWING WITH

00:05:59.091 --> 00:06:04.931
THE DRIVERS FOR SURE.
WE'RE ON WALNUT GROVE, WHICH IS

00:06:04.931 --> 00:06:09.001
VERY POPULAR FOR PEOPLE TO GET
TO AND FROM WORK AND ALREADY WE

00:06:09.001 --> 00:06:14.306
HAVE SEEN PEOPLE BE DEFEATED BY
THIS HILL HERE IN FRONT OF HOPE

00:06:14.306 --> 00:06:17.810
CHURCH IN WALNUT GROVE IN THE
CITY OF MEMPHIS.

00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:21.214
WE ACTUALLY SAW ABOUT TEN CARS
THAT EITHER HAD BEEN ABANDONED

00:06:21.214 --> 00:06:23.683
OR WRECKED.
YOU CAN SEE IT RIGHT HERE.

00:06:23.683 --> 00:06:27.220
ALREADY THIS MORNING IN THIS
SECTION WE HAVE SEEN FOUR CARS

00:06:27.220 --> 00:06:30.422
SPIN OUT OF CONTROL.
THAT CAR RIGHT THERE, THAT

00:06:30.422 --> 00:06:33.993
VEHICLE, THAT SUV IS THE LONE
ONE THAT IS JUST STUCK.

00:06:33.993 --> 00:06:37.864
IT CAN'T MOVE BECAUSE OF THE 

00:06:37.864 --> 00:06:39.732
ICE.
NOT ONLY IS THE ICE ON THIS ROAD

00:06:39.732 --> 00:06:42.835
HARD TO DRIVE ON BUT IT'S
ABSOLUTELY IMPOSSIBLE TO WALK

00:06:42.835 --> 00:06:46.639
ON.
I GOT A CHANCE MYSELF TO SEE FOR

00:06:46.639 --> 00:06:53.079
MYSELF THAT IT IS ICE.
ICE FOR SURE.

00:06:53.079 --> 00:06:56.615
FOR THE MOST PART PEOPLE ARE
HAVING TROUBLE GOING UP THE HILL

00:06:56.615 --> 00:06:59.719
AND ALSO DOWN THE HILL AS YOU
SEE THIS CRASHED OUT CAR RIGHT

00:06:59.719 --> 00:07:01.587
HERE.
ALSO WITH PEOPLE COMING DOWN

00:07:01.587 --> 00:07:06.092
THIS HILL RIGHT HERE, PEOPLE ARE
ENDING UP THAT HILL FOR SURE.

00:07:06.092 --> 00:07:10.663
SO I'VE BEEN IN CONTACT WITH
SEVERAL SOURCES AND WITH LOCAL

00:07:10.663 --> 00:07:13.199
HOSPITALS.
THANKFULLY NO ONE HAS SHOWN UP

00:07:13.199 --> 00:07:17.904
TO A HOSPITAL THIS MORNING DUE
TO INJURIES BECAUSE OF ANY OF

00:07:17.904 --> 00:07:23.843
THE CAR CRASHES THAT HAVE
HAPPENED OR BEING SPUN OUT OF

00:07:23.843 --> 00:07:26.579
CONTROL HERE IN THE CITY OF
MEMPHIS.

00:07:26.579 --> 00:07:32.218
DEFINITELY NOT A TYPICAL DAY.
IT'S COLD, EXTREMELY COLD, NOT

00:07:32.218 --> 00:07:35.588
WHAT YOU'RE USED TO IN THIS NECK
OF THE WOODS IN THE MID SOUTH

00:07:35.588 --> 00:07:40.793
AREA AND NOT A TYPICAL DRIVING
DAY FOR ANYONE WHO HAS TO GO TO

00:07:40.793 --> 00:07:43.729
OR FROM WORK.
&gt;&gt; MEMPHIS, THIS IS NOT YOUR

00:07:43.729 --> 00:07:46.165
WEATHER.
STAY HOME.

00:07:46.165 --> 00:07:47.933
&gt;&gt; AND JEREMY, DO NOT WALK ON
THAT ROAD.

00:07:47.933 --> 00:07:50.403
YOU CAN ACTUALLY SEE THE ICE,
RIGHT?

00:07:50.403 --> 00:07:53.873
IF YOUR CAMERAMAN WILL SHOW US
THAT SHOT AGAIN RIGHT NEXT TO

00:07:53.873 --> 00:07:56.909
YOU, YOU CAN SEE THE ICE ON THE
ROAD.

00:07:56.909 --> 00:08:01.814
DON'T DO IT, JEREMY.
&gt;&gt; Reporter: YOU CAN SEE THE

00:08:01.814 --> 00:08:03.816
ICE.
LOOK, I'M TOUCHING IT.

00:08:03.816 --> 00:08:07.019
UP SEE HOW SLICK MY HAND IS
RIGHT HERE.

00:08:07.019 --> 00:08:11.891
IT IS JUST SLIDING, SLICK AND
SLIDING.

00:08:11.891 --> 00:08:16.662
WHOO!
&gt;&gt; YEAH, THAT'S THE RIGHT WORD,

00:08:16.662 --> 00:08:18.230
WHOO!
JEREMY, THAT'S THE TRUEST THING

00:08:18.230 --> 00:08:23.703
THAT ANYBODY HAS SAID ON THIS
SHOW ALL MORNING.

00:08:23.703 --> 00:08:27.139
&gt;&gt; WHOO, WHOO!
&gt;&gt; NOW THAT IS A GOOD REPORT.

00:08:27.139 --> 00:08:30.543
WE WANT TO HEAD NOW TO DENVER
WHERE TEMPERATURES PLUMMETED

00:08:30.543 --> 00:08:34.413
OVERNIGHT AND WIND CHILLS ARE 13
DEGREES BELOW ZERO RIGHT NOW.

00:08:34.413 --> 00:08:36.949
THAT'S WHERE WE FIND LUCY
KAFANOV.

00:08:36.949 --> 00:08:39.685
GOOD MORNING TO YOU.
HOW ARE PEOPLE HOLDING UP AFTER

00:08:39.685 --> 00:08:42.855
SOME RECORD DROPS IN TEMPERATURE
THERE?

00:08:42.855 --> 00:08:45.891
&gt;&gt; Reporter: YEAH, DON.
GOOD MORNING TO YOU.

00:08:45.891 --> 00:08:49.729
NOT A GREAT MORNING CONSIDERING
HOW PAINFUL IT IS TO BE STANDING

00:08:49.729 --> 00:08:52.531
OUT HERE.
WE DID CONSIDER TRYING TO FIND

00:08:52.531 --> 00:08:56.335
FOLKS TO ASK THEM HOW THAT YOUR
HOLDING UP BUT THANKFULLY MOST

00:08:56.335 --> 00:08:59.639
PEOPLE SEEM TO BE HEEDING THE
ADVICE OF AUTHORITY AND STAYING

00:08:59.639 --> 00:09:01.307
OUT OF THIS TERRIBLE, BITTER
COLD.

00:09:01.307 --> 00:09:03.776
NOW COLORADO IS USED TO COLD
WINTERS.

00:09:03.776 --> 00:09:07.146
WE'RE USED TO SNOW, WE'RE USED
TO THE TEMPERATURES DROPPING BUT

00:09:07.146 --> 00:09:11.050
OF COURSE THE SWIFTNESS WITH
WHICH THIS ARCTIC BLAST CAME

00:09:11.050 --> 00:09:14.553
BARRELLING THROUGH WAS JUST
REMARKABLE WE'RE TALKING ABOUT A

00:09:14.553 --> 00:09:18.057
75-DEGREE TEMPERATURE SWING FROM
ROUGHLY 50 DEGREES ON WEDNESDAY

00:09:18.057 --> 00:09:22.962
WHEN I WAS ON AIR TO MINUS 24
DEGREES THURSDAY MORNING AND

00:09:22.962 --> 00:09:25.898
THOSE NUMBERS DON'T DO JUSTICE
TO HOW IT ACTUALLY FEELS TO THE

00:09:25.898 --> 00:09:30.403
HUMAN BODY, TO THE SKIN OUTSIDE.
WIND CHILLS OF NEGATIVE 60,

00:09:30.403 --> 00:09:34.273
APPROACHING NEGATIVE 60 IN SOME
PARTS OF COLORADO.

00:09:34.273 --> 00:09:38.678
THAT'S THE KIND OF CONDITION
THAT COULD CAUSE FROSTBITE TO

00:09:38.678 --> 00:09:43.515
EXPOSED SKIN IN MINUTES.
FOLKS ARE URGED TO STAY INDOORS.

00:09:43.515 --> 00:09:45.985
COLORADO'S GOVERNOR ACTIVATED
THE NATIONAL GUARD TO HELP WITH

00:09:45.985 --> 00:09:54.260
THE EXTREME COLD WEATHER
CONDITIONS WE DID SEE THE

00:09:54.260 --> 00:09:59.799
MASSIVE DENVER COLISEUM OPEN UP
TO GET OUT OF THE COLD.

00:09:59.799 --> 00:10:03.436
THERE WAS SO MUCH DEMAND, THEY
HAD TO OPEN UP TWO MORE CENTERS

00:10:03.436 --> 00:10:06.338
TO KEEP PEOPLE OUT OF THE
UNCOMFORTABLE, PAINFUL

00:10:06.338 --> 00:10:08.441
CONDITIONS.
MOST OF THE CITY IS HUNKERING

00:10:08.441 --> 00:10:10.242
DOWN.
WE ARE SEEING CAR TRAFFIC AND

00:10:10.242 --> 00:10:12.645
THERE IS GOOD NEWS ON THE
HORIZON FOR US.

00:10:12.645 --> 00:10:18.417
WE'RE EXPECTING THESE COLD WIND
CHILLS UNTIL ABOUT 11 A.M. LOCAL

00:10:18.417 --> 00:10:22.388
TIME BUT THEN THE TEMPERATURES
WILL FINALLY START CLIMBING

00:10:22.388 --> 00:10:26.158
ABOVE ZERO.
WE'VE HAD 35 HOURS OF

00:10:26.158 --> 00:10:30.830
TEMPERATURES BELOW ZERO.
WE COULD BE BACK TO REGULAR

00:10:30.830 --> 00:10:35.368
TEMPERATURES BY CHRISTMAS.
&gt;&gt; LUCY KAFANOV, THANK YOU

